## The 4-Layer Clean Architecture Specification

Every enterprise mobile codebase—whether implemented in Kotlin, Swift, or TypeScript—must strictly adhere to the 4 architectural layers described below:

<div class="portal-table-wrap">
  <table class="portal-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Architectural Layer</th>
        <th>Primary Responsibilities</th>
        <th>Allowed Inward Dependencies</th>
        <th>Prohibited Elements</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>1. Presentation Layer</strong></td>
        <td>Renders reactive UI views, captures user input, and manages screen lifecycle state.</td>
        <td>Depends only on the <strong>Domain Layer</strong> (executes Use Cases and observes state).</td>
        <td>No direct SQL queries, no direct HTTP client calls, no raw network DTO models.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>2. Domain Layer</strong></td>
        <td>Encapsulates pure enterprise business rules, entity models, and abstract repository contracts.</td>
        <td><strong>Zero external dependencies.</strong> Pure language code (zero Android, iOS, or React imports).</td>
        <td>No UI widgets, no database drivers, no third-party SDK dependencies, no platform imports.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>3. Data Layer</strong></td>
        <td>Implements domain repository contracts. Coordinates remote APIs with offline local databases.</td>
        <td>Depends on the <strong>Domain Layer</strong> (implements interfaces) and <strong>Infrastructure</strong>.</td>
        <td>No direct UI rendering logic, no lifecycle observation, no business rule mutation.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>4. Infrastructure / Core</strong></td>
        <td>Provides foundational cross-cutting capabilities (SSO Auth, Circuit Breaker, Datadog RUM, KeyStore).</td>
        <td>Standalone shared packages consumed by the Data and Presentation layers.</td>
        <td>No feature-specific business domain logic. Must remain reusable across repositories.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

