## Dependency Inversion & Data Flow Diagram

The **Dependency Rule** dictates that source code dependencies must only point inward toward higher-level business logic. The Domain layer is the core of the system and knows nothing about databases, network protocols, or UI widgets:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph Client["1. Presentation Layer"]
        UI["UI Views\n(SwiftUI / Jetpack Compose / React Native)"]
        VM["State Holders\n(ViewModels / React Hooks / State Machines)"]
        UI -->|"User Event"| VM
    end

    subgraph CoreDomain["2. Domain Layer (Pure Business Core)"]
        UC["Use Cases & Interactors\n(e.g., SubmitOrderUseCase)"]
        Entities["Pure Business Entities\n(e.g., Order, LineItem, User)"]
        RepoContract["Repository Interfaces\n(e.g., OrderRepository Contract)"]
        VM -->|"Executes"| UC
        UC -->|"Operates On"| Entities
        UC -->|"Invokes Contract"| RepoContract
    end

    subgraph DataInfra["3. Data & Infrastructure Layer"]
        RepoImpl["Repository Implementation\n(e.g., OrderRepositoryImpl)"]
        LocalSource["Local Offline Cache\n(Room SQLite / CoreData / MMKV)"]
        RemoteSource["Remote API Client\n(Circuit Breaker + Auth Headers)"]
        RepoImpl -.->|"Implements"| RepoContract
        RepoImpl -->|"Read / Write"| LocalSource
        RepoImpl -->|"HTTP Network"| RemoteSource
    end

