## Architectural Anti-Patterns & Prohibitions

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">ARCHITECTURAL BOUNDARY PROHIBITIONS</div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>1. UI Calling Data Sources Directly:</strong> Never call SQLite queries, network endpoints, or KeyStore methods directly from a SwiftUI View, Jetpack Compose Composable, or React component. All access must be brokered through a Domain Use Case.</li>
    <li><strong>2. Platform Frameworks in Domain:</strong> The Domain layer must never import <code>android.*</code>, <code>UIKit</code>, <code>SwiftUI</code>, or <code>react-native</code>. Pure business logic must remain 100% portable and unit testable in pure JVM or native runtimes.</li>
    <li><strong>3. Leaking Network DTOs to the UI:</strong> Remote JSON DTOs must be transformed by Data Mappers into immutable Domain Entities before leaving the Data layer. This insulates UI screens from backend API breaking changes.</li>
    <li><strong>4. God ViewModels / Fat Controllers:</strong> ViewModels must only coordinate UI state and invoke Use Cases. Business validation, multi-source orchestration, and caching logic belong strictly in Use Cases and Repositories.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

